// @contract: C-331
// The self-hosted zlib surface (#1700): DECODING is byte-identical across
// legs by construction (DEFLATE decoding is exact) — the three vectors below
// were produced by the NATIVE flate2 encoder (dynamic-Huffman zlib/deflate
// and the gzip container) and must decode to the same text on every leg.
// COMPRESSED bytes are leg-dependent by design (native flate2, wasm stored
// blocks) — the bounded divergence C-331 declares — so the encode half is
// pinned by ROUND TRIP on whichever leg runs, never by encoded bytes.
// crc32/adler32 live in spec/stdlib/zlib_test.almd — the interp leg has no
// arm for them yet, and a mid-fixture abstention would cost the decode half
// its third vote.
import zlib

